   "definition_quote": "We consider continuous bandit problems where the set of arms is the interval $[0,1]$, and where the expected reward $\\mu$ is a continuous and unimodal function of the arm. More precisely, there exists $x^\\star$ such that $x\\mapsto \\mu(x)$ is strictly increasing (resp. decreasing) in $[0,x^\\star]$ (resp. in $[x^\\star, 1]$)."
